    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on maximizing efficiency against mid-rotation arms while navigating the persistent scarcity of stolen bases. **Kyle Tucker** (65.99) and **Sam Antonacci** (64.49) headline our offensive efforts. **Kyle Tucker** remains a plug-and-play staple despite the presence of Ray, as his elite base projection holds strong, while **Sam Antonacci** provides immense value out of the leadoff spot; his combination of a favorable matchup against Lugo and a high .391 xwOBA suggests he is the primary candidate to drive our production in both Runs and SB today. **Gunnar Henderson** (59.34) and **Andy Pages** (59.04) represent our next tier of high-impact starters, with **Gunnar Henderson** benefiting significantly from park factors that offset the difficulty of facing a sharp arm like Fried.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, prioritizing daily efficiency to preserve game caps. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. While his raw hitting profile is among the team's best, the optimization model correctly identified that the combination of a difficult matchup against Jax and the higher efficiency floors provided by **Coby Mayo** and **Nasim Nunez** in their respective spots made them the mathematically sound choice for today\u2019s constraints. We are closely monitoring the lineup status for **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks**, both of whom are projected as marginal starts; should their respective orders drop, we may look to consolidate our remaining games. We continue to manage the long-term absences of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, whose IL statuses continue to limit our positional flexibility, leaving **Brady House** on the outside looking in as we favor the active platoon advantages provided by **Jackson Merrill** and **Miguel Vargas**.",
